  "notes": "Thick lines inside the streets are water pipes (with hydrant dots), not street edges; centres are taken between lot lines. Ringwalt and Greendale: suffix not printed inside or near the strip. Ringwalt merges into Clifton Avenue at an acute angle; the pick is where the two centrelines meet (Ringwalt's south edge runs level to about x 5900). Lafayette Avenue is printed west of Clifton Avenue (label near x 2200, y 4580); the unlabelled 40 ft stem east of Clifton to the loop is taken as Lafayette Avenue; the pick at 6145,3382 is the fork where the Lafayette Circle loop closes on the stem. The three '?' picks are narrow unnamed lanes (printed LOT 'A', about 12-20 ft, with a 4 in/6 in water pipe) ringing the M. J. Roche & Thos. J. Dyer subdivision west of Clifton Avenue; they may be private. The 60 ft street along the bottom edge has only 'AVENUE' printed near the strip; taken as McAlpin Avenue from the plate description. Steps (printed STEPS) run from Severn Avenue near x 6690 north to Lafayette Circle: not a street. A dashed PRIVATE DRIVE east of Clifton Avenue near 6700,1950 is not a street. At the top edge the tan bands beside Clifton Avenue (east of 6290,520 and west of 6170,480) are plate margin, not streets. Amazon Avenue is narrower east of Egbert Avenue than west of it."
